# API keys / secrets - NEVER commit active keys
#
# v2 keeps its settings module in git on purpose: v2/backend/app/core/config.py
# holds no credentials. Every secret lives in v2/backend/.env, which is ignored
# below, and the committed template is v2/backend/.env.example.
#
# The previous blanket `config.py` / `**/config.py` rules excluded that module,
# so a fresh clone crashed at `from app.core.config import settings` in
# app/main.py, app/intelligence/provider.py and app/behavior/baseline.py.
#
# The legacy v1 tree still ships credential-bearing modules; anchor the ignores
# to it instead of matching every path named config.py in the repository.
v1/**/config.py
v1/**/key_pool.py
section1_firms/config.py
section4_vision_ai/config.py
section5_pipeline/config.py
section5_pipeline/key_pool.py

